-- title:
--   Dimension $3$
-- statement:
--   **The rung $r=3$ of Challenge 7: the Kepler conjecture.** The sphere-packing constant of $\mathbb R^3$ equals its lattice-packing constant:
--
--   $$\Delta_3=\Delta_3^L .$$
--
--   Both equal $\pi/\sqrt{18}$, attained by the face-centred cubic lattice.
-- source:
--   T. C. Hales, A proof of the Kepler conjecture, Ann. of Math. 162 (2005), 1065–1185, https://doi.org/10.4007/annals.2005.162.1065; formal proof in T. Hales et al., A formal proof of the Kepler conjecture, Forum Math. Pi 5 (2017), https://doi.org/10.1017/fmp.2017.1

